      "message": "Note that this is the first place I\u0027ve directly run into the conflict between the abomination that is \"associated headers\" in iwyu and the current \"clang tidy\" expectation for each file to actually include what it uses. This file (`SkCodec.cpp`) is not including `SkSpan.h` and iwyu currently likes it that way because there is a header named `SkCodec.h` which does include `SkSpan.h`. We need a flag in iwyu to turn off associated headers. Looks like this is https://github.com/include-what-you-use/include-what-you-use/issues/919 . It actually shouldn\u0027t bee too difficult to fix this (just don\u0027t automatically add to the list), so maybe I\u0027ll take a look into that.",
